{title: Requium}
{artist: Keshi}
{key: Db}
{Capo: 1}

{start_of_grid: Intro}
| Em7 . . . | Bb7 . . . | Em7 . . . | Bb7 . . . |
{end_of_grid}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The [C]sun and the [C+5]moon, they [Am/C]just won’t stop for [C7]you,
[F]dancing a[Fm]round like nothing [C]changed.  [C]
I [C]try not to [C+5]move, a [Am/C]fight I always [C7]lose,
[F]time always [Bb7]seems to find a [C]way.    [Dm7]Oh,  [C7/E]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
It’s [F]not the [Bb7]same, I [Am]miss you every[D7]day,
[F]still some things I [Bb7]wish I told [C]ya.    [Dm7]      [C7/E]
[F]Can’t you [Bb7]stay, [Am]why’d you go a[D7]way,
I [F]hope that we can [Bb7]do it o - ver. [C]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_grid: Interlude}
| Em7 . . . | Bb7 . . . | Em7 . . . | Bb7 . . . |
{end_of_grid}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I [C]cried and I [C+5]begged: take [Am/C]someone else in[C7]stead,
[F]not that he [Fm]listens any[C]way.      [C]
[C]Stairs I can’t [C+5]  tread, so, [Am/C]you go on a[C7]head,
[F]oh, I know [Bb7]you won’t mind the [C]wait.   [Dm7]Oh,  [C7/E]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge: End-Chorus}
It’s [F]not the [Bb7]same, I [Am]miss you every[D7]day,
[F]still some things I [Bb7]wish I told [C]ya.    [Dm7]     [C7/E]
[F]Can’t you [Bb7]stay, [Am]why’d you go a[D7]way,
I [F]hope that we can [Bb7]do it o - ver. [C]
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_grid: Outro}
| C . . . | C+5 . . . | Am/C . . . | C+5 . . . ||
{end_of_grid}
